      "stolen_check": false,
      "study_text": "<p>A variation of the Paryashera Monster that roams the Winterlands Ocean. Also known as <strong>\"The Diving Steam\"</strong> This species makes its lair in undersea volcanoes, developing hot, magma-like calluses. It is capable of releasing heated steam and has a strong affinity with the fire element.</p>",
      "subtype": "Sub-Type",
      "subtype_list": "REPTILIAN",
      "sword_ef": "100",
      "sword_vu": "NA",
      "tactic_notes": "<div align=\"left\">\n<h2>1. Play around with your food</h2>\n<p><strong>Molten Paryashera</strong> has 5 basic attacks with no specific combo. These attacks deals damage and apply some inconvenience with its debuff. Use these move to let the player relax.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>⚔️ Peck : Chain(2) and Pierce.</li>\n<li>⚔️ Tail Slap : Multi(2) with Delay.</li>\n<li>⚔️ Heat Claw : A single target attack with Burn.</li>\n<li>🏹 Lava Splash : A single target range attack with Petrify.</li>\n<li>🏹 Rock Drop : A single target range Earth attack with confusion.</li>\n<li>⚡Vapor Shot : Can target up to 2 creatures and may apply <strong>Turbulence</strong>, which may come into play later.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2. Core attack: Thrashing and Head-On tackle</h2>\n<p><strong>Molten Paryashera</strong>'s core combo: Use either <strong>⚔️ Thrashing&nbsp;</strong>or&nbsp;<strong>⚔️ Spin Thrashing</strong> to deals Overflow damage then mark a target. On the next turn, depending on previous attack, follow up with <strong>⚔️ Head-On Crash</strong> or&nbsp;<strong>⚔️ Head-On Drill.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>⚔️ Thrashing &gt; ⚔️ Head-On Crash</strong> :&nbsp;Deals massive damage to <strong>Guard</strong>less<strong>&nbsp;</strong>creature</li>\n<li><strong>⚔️ Spin Thrashing &gt; ⚔️ Head-on Drill</strong> : Prevent <strong>Guard</strong>ed<strong>&nbsp;</strong>from performing <strong>Guard</strong> again via applying <strong>Stagger</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Use these two alternative at least once to teach this mechanic to the player. Use this combo once every other turn (depend on the fight progression).</p>\n<h2>3. Play time is over. It's ZERO POWER TIME!</h2>\n<p><strong>Molten Paryashera</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>fills its<strong> Zero Power</strong> clock by hitting any of its<strong> Head-On</strong> attack. Hitting twice will fill the clock and, with its Zero Power action, place <strong>Molten Vapor</strong> clock.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Molten Vapor&nbsp;</strong>clock has 6 section. While it is in the scene, <strong>Molten Paryashera</strong>'s<strong> </strong>attacks<strong> </strong>becomes far more deadly and vicious by allows it to go <strong>Hidden</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Molten Vapor&nbsp;</strong>clock will be filled automatically at the end of each round. It is also filled when Air damage is dealt during the conflict.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the start of each round, ⚡<strong>Heat Steam</strong> may be used for free (no turn and Mind Points required). ⚡<strong>Heat Steam,</strong> other than dealing damage, puts <strong>Molten Paryashera&nbsp;</strong>in <strong>Hidden </strong>buff until its next attack, increase the potent of the attack. It also improve its core mechanic and introduce new attacks:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>While <strong>Hidden</strong>, instead of <strong>⚔️ Thrashing</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>or <strong>⚔️ Spin Thrashing</strong>, the boss may perform <strong>⚔️ Unknown Thrashing,&nbsp;</strong>which hide the name of the next attack as well as the target creature.</li>\n<li>Use<strong> Ambusher's Focus</strong> to guarantee any attack out of <strong>Hidden</strong>. This stay until the end of scene but can be dispel. Using&nbsp;<strong>Ambusher's Focus&nbsp;</strong>while <strong>Hidden&nbsp;</strong>will not remove the buff, as it is not counted as an Attack.</li>\n<li>⚡<strong>Vapor Shot</strong> can be used<strong>&nbsp;</strong>to deal <strong>Air</strong> damage in order to manipulate <strong>Molten Vapor&nbsp;</strong>clock. This attack also deals more damage as more section of the clock is filled.</li>\n<li>Aim to fill the&nbsp;<strong>Molten Vapor&nbsp;</strong>clock before the boss run out of action, so that the boss can use <strong>Molten Vapor Burst</strong>, a massive attack that <strong>Burn </strong>every target it hit.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>4. Misc.</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The boss has no Mind Points recovery skill. Spend Ultima points to refill Mind Points and clear all debuff if it improve the player experience.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
